opengl32: the legacy ChoosePixelFormat no longer returns floating-point formats (Neutron#57)

What the reporter saw: "After Effects 2026 freezes permanently when OCIO color management (built-in or custom ACES config) is
enabled while footage is in the project."

Mechanism (ae57f, lab): After Effects' hidden OpenColorIO window ("OpenColorIO_Win_Class", 113x18) calls the legacy
ChoosePixelFormat with DRAW_TO_WINDOW|SUPPORT_OPENGL|DOUBLEBUFFER, RGBA, cColorBits 128, depth 32, stencil 32. Our legacy list
holds every EGL config that can draw to a window, so NVIDIA's RGBA16F configs appear as "RGBA, 64 color bits" and win (format
135 of 138). SetPixelFormat then needs a float16 Wayland EGL window surface. The reporter's log shows that drawable never
arriving for that one window; when the lab makes that creation fail or block (LD_PRELOAD shim), After Effects freezes at the
first import under OCIO exactly as reported (4/4; 0/3 without the shim). Why it does not arrive on his RTX 3060 / 620.70.06 /
Fedora 45 is not known.

Windows behavior (measured, probe round 51, owner's box, RTX 5070): the legacy list ALSO holds the eight float formats (89-92 and
their twins, "RGBA, 64 color bits", WGL type 0x21a0), but ChoosePixelFormat with the After Effects request returns format 11, an
8-bit format (RGB a0, depth 24, stencil 8). Windows never hands the legacy caller a float format.

Fix: wglChoosePixelFormat skips formats whose WGL pixel type is float (RGBA_FLOAT_ARB / RGBA_UNSIGNED_FLOAT_EXT). The OCIO
window then gets format 70 (RGBA8, depth 24, stencil 8) like every other After Effects GL window. Format numbering,
DescribePixelFormat and wglChoosePixelFormatARB are untouched (the list stays as it is, as on Windows). On NVIDIA the only legacy
formats above 32 bits are the float ones, so "skip float" and "never exceed the screen depth" pick the same format there. Windows
also picked an a0 format where Wine picks RGBA8; that stays as is. Kill switch: NEUTRON_GL_LEGACY_NO_FLOAT=0.

Not covered: an app that walks DescribePixelFormat itself can still pick a float format (Windows lists them too). Non-float
formats above 32 bits (Mesa's RGBA16 UNORM, seen in 32-bit llvmpipe) stay selectable.

Lab evidence (11.10-224pf = 224 + this opengl32.dll x86_64 + i386; glfloat/NOTES.md): probe 224 -> 135 float n=2, 224pf -> 70
n=2, kill switch -> 135 n=2 (64-bit; the 32-bit process runs on llvmpipe here, no float configs, 154 in every arm).
After Effects 168 dpi OCIO + import + comp + preview: 224 and 224pf both work; only change: the OCIO window's format 135 -> 70.
Photoshop (zoom/rotate), Illustrator GPU Preview, Lightroom Classic Develop, FL Studio call the legacy chooser too and already got
8-bit formats: unchanged, 0 px.
---
--- a/dlls/opengl32/wgl.c
+++ b/dlls/opengl32/wgl.c
@@ -541,12 +541,35 @@
 /***********************************************************************
  *		wglChoosePixelFormat (OPENGL32.@)
  */
+/* NEUTRON: the legacy chooser never offers a floating-point format. A PIXELFORMATDESCRIPTOR cannot describe one (its
+ * iPixelType is RGBA or COLORINDEX only); on Windows float formats are reached through wglChoosePixelFormatARB with
+ * WGL_TYPE_RGBA_FLOAT_ARB. Here every EGL config that can draw to a window is in the list, so NVIDIA's RGBA16F configs
+ * showed up as "RGBA, 64 color bits" and won any request for more than 32 color bits. After Effects' hidden OpenColorIO
+ * window asks for cColorBits 128 and got one, i.e. a float16 Wayland window surface that not every driver/compositor
+ * pair delivers; when that drawable does not come back After Effects freezes at the first footage under OCIO (Neutron#57).
+ * Kill switch NEUTRON_GL_LEGACY_NO_FLOAT=0. */
+static BOOL neutron_legacy_no_float(void)
+{
+    static int on = -1;
+    if (on < 0)
+    {
+        const char *e = getenv( "NEUTRON_GL_LEGACY_NO_FLOAT" );
+        on = e ? (e[0] != '0') : 1;
+        ERR( "neutron-gateresolved: NEUTRON_GL_LEGACY_NO_FLOAT = %d (%s)\n", on, e ? "environment" : "default" );
+    }
+    return on;
+}
+
+static struct wgl_pixel_format *get_pixel_formats( HDC hdc, UINT *num_formats, UINT *num_onscreen_formats );
+
 INT WINAPI wglChoosePixelFormat(HDC hdc, const PIXELFORMATDESCRIPTOR* ppfd)
 {
     PIXELFORMATDESCRIPTOR format, best;
     int i, count, best_format;
     int bestDBuffer = -1, bestStereo = -1;
     DWORD is_memdc;
+    struct wgl_pixel_format *wgl_formats;
+    UINT num_wgl_formats = 0, num_wgl_onscreen = 0;
 
     TRACE( "%p %p: size %u version %u flags %lu type %u color %u %u,%u,%u,%u "
            "accum %u depth %u stencil %u aux %u\n",
@@ -568,10 +591,20 @@
     best.cAuxBuffers = -1;
     best.cAccumBits = -1;
 
+    wgl_formats = neutron_legacy_no_float() ? get_pixel_formats( hdc, &num_wgl_formats, &num_wgl_onscreen ) : NULL;
+
     for (i = 1; i <= count; i++)
     {
         if (!wglDescribePixelFormat( hdc, i, sizeof(format), &format )) continue;
 
+        if (wgl_formats && i <= num_wgl_formats &&
+            (wgl_formats[i - 1].pixel_type == WGL_TYPE_RGBA_FLOAT_ARB ||
+             wgl_formats[i - 1].pixel_type == WGL_TYPE_RGBA_UNSIGNED_FLOAT_EXT))
+        {
+            TRACE( "float format skipped for iPixelFormat=%d\n", i );
+            continue;
+        }
+
         if ((ppfd->iPixelType == PFD_TYPE_COLORINDEX) != (format.iPixelType == PFD_TYPE_COLORINDEX))
         {
             TRACE( "pixel type mismatch for iPixelFormat=%d\n", i );
